\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Three-trajectory structural and temporal anatomy of the 11 Transformer second moments (\texttt  {130M}).} \textbf  {(a)} Pythagorean diagonal anisotropy share ($\mathrm  {DiagAniso}$) across Muon, MuonT, and WT-MLP-Lag consistently separates coordinate-dominated $d_{\mathrm  {ff}}=2048$ MLP outputs (\texttt  {out:gate} $80.6\%$--$89.5\%$, \texttt  {out:up} $77.9\%$--$90.8\%$) from rotation-dominated $d_{\mathrm  {model}}=512$ residual outputs (\texttt  {out:o, down} $0.8\%$--$1.0\%$) and inputs. \textbf  {(b)} Backward cotangent top-16 eigenspaces drift an order of magnitude faster over 250 steps than RMSNormed forward activations across all three trajectories ($16\times $--$32\times $ faster on \texttt  {out:v} vs.\ \texttt  {in:attn}). \textbf  {(c)} Rapid subspace drift causes Toner's cached-eigenbasis root solver on Null-Dense (MuonT) to trigger $107{,}911$ exact eigendecomposition fallbacks on dense outputs ($22.1/\text  {step}$) vs.\ only $369$ ($29$ post-warmup) on inputs.}}{7}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:structural_audit}{{2}{7}{\textbf {Three-trajectory structural and temporal anatomy of the 11 Transformer second moments (\texttt {130M}).} \textbf {(a)} Pythagorean diagonal anisotropy share ($\mathrm {DiagAniso}$) across \mname {Muon}, \mname {MuonT}, and \mname {WT-MLP-Lag} consistently separates coordinate-dominated $\dff =2048$ MLP outputs (\texttt {out:gate} $80.6\%$--$89.5\%$, \texttt {out:up} $77.9\%$--$90.8\%$) from rotation-dominated $\dm =512$ residual outputs (\texttt {out:o, down} $0.8\%$--$1.0\%$) and inputs. \textbf {(b)} Backward cotangent top-16 eigenspaces drift an order of magnitude faster over 250 steps than RMSNormed forward activations across all three trajectories ($16\times $--$32\times $ faster on \texttt {out:v} vs.\ \texttt {in:attn}). \textbf {(c)} Rapid subspace drift causes Toner's cached-eigenbasis root solver on \mname {Null-Dense} (\mname {MuonT}) to trigger $107{,}911$ exact eigendecomposition fallbacks on dense outputs ($22.1/\text {step}$) vs.\ only $369$ ($29$ post-warmup) on inputs}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\newlabel{fig:structural_audit@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][7][]7}{}{}{}}
