\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Master confirmatory and scaling results across model sizes, token horizons, and evaluation suites} on the unified \texttt  {fast\_lag} runner. $\Delta $ columns report differences relative to same-regime Muon (negative means lower cross-entropy loss in nats); the penultimate column repeats the final-$\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$ difference against same-regime MuonT, the strongest prior method, since that is the comparison the method is designed to improve on. ``Late Mean $\Delta \mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$'' averages every evaluation checkpoint in the second half of training ($11$ per run) with checkpoint win counts in parentheses. ``Paloma 16-Dom.'' reports the unweighted macro mean across all 16 Paloma subsets with domain win counts vs.\ Muon. ``Step (s), $\Delta t$'' across all four phases reports unified optimized steady-state mid-training benchmark latencies ($8\times \text  {A100}$, $\text  {mb}=4$ at \texttt  {130M} [\Cref  {tab:bench19}]; $32\times \text  {A100}$ RDMA, $\text  {mb}=2, \texttt  {chunk}=2$ at \texttt  {520M}, or $4.642 / 4.894 / 4.986 / 5.322\text  { s}$ on $1\times 8\text  { A100}$ [\Cref  {tab:bench520m}]). $^\dagger $In Phase 2, pre-registered Gate 1 locked MuonT to $0.016$ and OD-All/WT-MLP-Lag to $0.02263$ (conservative against WT-MLP-Lag; mid-decay LRs therefore differ).}}{14}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
