\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Multi-seed confirmation, $4\times $ Chinchilla overtraining, and \texttt  {520M} width scaling.} \textbf  {(a)} Across fresh paired \texttt  {seeds 1, 2, 3} at \texttt  {130M} ($2.68\text  {B}$ tokens), paired loss reduction against same-seed Muon for all three arms (individual seeds as open circles). WT-MLP-Lag recovers $-0.0153$ to $-0.0155$ nats where input-only MuonT recovers $-0.0115$ to $-0.0119$, and beats tuned MuonT on $3/3$ seeds across $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$, $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {C4}}$, and 16-domain Paloma. \textbf  {(b, c)} Trajectories are plotted against same-regime MuonT rather than Muon, because the Muon gap ($+10.3$ and $+6.5 \times 10^{-3}$, grey dashed) is large enough to compress the differences of interest to invisibility; Muon is shown as a curve for scale. \textbf  {(b)} Under $4\times $ Chinchilla overtraining ($80$ TPP, $10.74\text  {B}$ tokens), matched-LR WT-MLP-Lag beats MuonT at all $11$ second-half checkpoints (shaded region, mean $-0.00444$ nats), whereas running $41\%$ hotter ($\sqrt  {2}\times $, coral dotted curve) induces a transient mid-decay penalty that masks the geometric benefit. \textbf  {(c)} Scaling width $2\times $ to \texttt  {520M} ($d=1{,}024$, $10.74\text  {B}$ tokens, official pinned $\eta =0.02263$) leaves pure-diagonal OD-All behind MuonT ($+0.00058$ final, though still $-0.00588$ against Muon), whereas WT-MLP-Lag stays strictly below MuonT at all $11$ second-half checkpoints (mean $-0.00309$ nats).}}{16}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scaling_traj}{{5}{16}{\textbf {Multi-seed confirmation, $4\times $ Chinchilla overtraining, and \texttt {520M} width scaling.} \textbf {(a)} Across fresh paired \texttt {seeds 1, 2, 3} at \texttt {130M} ($2.68\text {B}$ tokens), paired loss reduction against same-seed \mname {Muon} for all three arms (individual seeds as open circles). \mname {WT-MLP-Lag} recovers $-0.0153$ to $-0.0155$ nats where input-only \mname {MuonT} recovers $-0.0115$ to $-0.0119$, and beats tuned \mname {MuonT} on $3/3$ seeds across $\Lsel $, $\Lc $, and 16-domain Paloma. \textbf {(b, c)} Trajectories are plotted against same-regime \mname {MuonT} rather than \mname {Muon}, because the \mname {Muon} gap ($+10.3$ and $+6.5 \times 10^{-3}$, grey dashed) is large enough to compress the differences of interest to invisibility; \mname {Muon} is shown as a curve for scale. \textbf {(b)} Under $4\times $ Chinchilla overtraining ($80$ TPP, $10.74\text {B}$ tokens), matched-LR \mname {WT-MLP-Lag} beats \mname {MuonT} at all $11$ second-half checkpoints (shaded region, mean $-0.00444$ nats), whereas running $41\%$ hotter ($\sqrt {2}\times $, coral dotted curve) induces a transient mid-decay penalty that masks the geometric benefit. \textbf {(c)} Scaling width $2\times $ to \texttt {520M} ($d=1{,}024$, $10.74\text {B}$ tokens, official pinned $\eta =0.02263$) leaves pure-diagonal \mname {OD-All} behind \mname {MuonT} ($+0.00058$ final, though still $-0.00588$ against \mname {Muon}), whereas \mname {WT-MLP-Lag} stays strictly below \mname {MuonT} at all $11$ second-half checkpoints (mean $-0.00309$ nats)}{figure.caption.23}{}}
\newlabel{fig:scaling_traj@cref}{{[figure][5][]5}{[1][15][]16}{}{}{}}
