\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Design-space ablations and multi-seed comparison against recent polar preconditioners.} Unlike \Cref  {tab:main_scaling}, differences here are reported against same-wave MuonT: these arms vary only the output-side operator at a fixed dense input side, so MuonT is the controlled reference. For reference, MuonT itself is $-0.0119$ nats below Muon in this regime. \textbf  {(a)} Late-half $\Delta \mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$ vs.\ MuonT across 14 controlled configurations at \texttt  {130M} ($2.68\text  {B}$ tokens), showing that dropping input whitening (Abl-OutOnly, Abl-BothDiag) degrades loss, whereas width-thresholded WT-MLP and WT-MLP-Lag match or exceed full dense DT-All. \textbf  {(b)} Paired held-out $\Delta \mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$ vs.\ Muon (mean across fresh \texttt  {seeds 1 \& 2}, isotropic matrix decay, $\eta = 0.032$). Inset shows 9-step smoothed early training loss deltas ($\text  {steps } 1\text  {--}300$): GO-MUON plunges $-0.57$ nats by step $18$ before crossing above Muon around step $200$ and finishing $+0.031\text  {--}0.032$ nats worse, while Mousse tracks Muon ($\pm 0.003$) and WT-MLP maintains a steady $-0.010$-nat lead.}}{20}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
